# Barco ClickShare CX Driver (REST API V2)
#
# Controls Barco ClickShare CX-series Base Units over the local REST API V2
# (HTTPS, port 4003). ClickShare is a wireless presentation system — laptops
# and mobile devices share content to the Base Unit, which composes it onto
# a connected display.
#
# Models covered (CX / C / CB-series):
#   - CX-20, CX-30, CX-50 (Gen1 + Gen2)
#   - C-5, C-10, C-10A
#   - CB-Core, CB-Pro
# All run the same V2 REST API on the same TCP port. The doc is identical
# across the family — feature differences (number of buttons, video outputs,
# UVC pass-through availability) are reported by the Base Unit at runtime
# via the `supportedOutputs`, `supportedModes`, etc. arrays.
#
# Protocol reference:
#   Barco "ClickShare REST API — Reference manual", R5915531 /12 (2025-10-29).
#   Available from Barco's product documentation portal alongside the firmware.
#   In-Base-Unit OpenAPI explorer: https://<base-unit>:4003/api-docs
#   Version listing endpoints: /supportedVersions, /currentVersion (no auth).
#
# Authentication:
#   HTTP Basic. Default credentials are integrator/integrator. They are
#   changed in the Base Unit's web Configurator; supply whatever the site
#   uses in this device's config.
#
# TLS:
#   The Base Unit ships a self-signed certificate. `verify_ssl: false` by
#   default — the integrator can replace the cert with a trusted one and
#   flip verify_ssl to true. There is no plain-HTTP endpoint.
#
# Push vs poll:
#   The V2 API supports SSE subscriptions (Accept: text/event-stream keeps
#   the connection open and pushes updates) per §1.1 of the spec. The
#   platform's HTTP transport is request/response only today, so this
#   driver polls. The endpoints we poll are cheap and the cadence is 30 s
#   by default — fast enough for "is anyone presenting right now?" use
#   cases. Subscription support is a future platform improvement (tracked
#   alongside other push-deferred drivers).
#
# Scope:
#   Universal AV-integrator runtime control surface — system status (in_use
#   / sharing / uptime / errors), standby + wake + reboot, audio enable /
#   output selection, video mode (Extended/Clone) + CEC toggle, wallpaper
#   selection, paired-button readback, power-management settings.
#   Install-time configuration (network, wireless, ClickShare app config,
#   peripherals, certificates, signage, Flexible Room System pairing) is
#   intentionally NOT exposed — those belong in the web Configurator and
#   Barco's XMS fleet management product.

id: barco_clickshare_cx
name: Barco ClickShare CX
manufacturer: Barco
category: streaming
version: 1.2.3
author: OpenAVC
description: >
  Wireless presentation Base Unit control via local REST API V2 (HTTPS,
  port 4003). System status, standby / wake / reboot, audio + video +
  wallpaper + CEC, paired-button readback. Covers CX-20 / CX-30 / CX-50,
  C-5 / C-10 / C-10A, CB-Core / CB-Pro.

source_url: https://www.barco.com/services/website/en/TdeFiles/Download?FileNumber=R5915531&TdeType=3&MajorVersion=12
tags: [barco, clickshare, wireless-presentation, byod, cx, c-series, cb-series]
verified: false
simulated: true
protocols: [clickshare_v2]
ports: [4003]

compatible_models:
  - manufacturer: Barco
    models:
      - ClickShare CX-20
      - ClickShare CX-20 Gen2
      - ClickShare CX-30
      - ClickShare CX-30 Gen2
      - ClickShare CX-50
      - ClickShare CX-50 Gen2
      - ClickShare C-5
      - ClickShare C-10
      - ClickShare C-10A
      - ClickShare CB-Core
      - ClickShare CB-Pro
    confidence: untested
    notes: >
      Same V2 REST API across the entire CX / C / CB family. Feature
      differences (number of paired buttons, dual video outputs on CX-50
      Gen2, UVC pass-through on CX-30 Gen2 / CX-50 Gen2) are reported
      by the Base Unit at runtime in the `supportedOutputs`, `supportedModes`,
      `supportedPowerModes`, etc. arrays — the driver doesn't need to know
      the model. Older CSE / CSC ClickShare units use a different (legacy)
      API and are NOT covered.

transport: http

help:
  overview: >
    The ClickShare Base Unit exposes a local REST API on port 4003 (HTTPS).
    Use this driver to mirror runtime status (is anyone sharing?), force
    the Base Unit into / out of standby, reboot, and switch audio output /
    wallpaper / video mode under macro control. Typical room logic: when
    the room shutdown macro fires, send `standby`; when the room comes up,
    send `wakeup` (or rely on the Base Unit's auto-wake on first share).
  setup: >
    1. Set a static IP (or DHCP reservation) on the Base Unit — its
       Ethernet MAC is on the bottom label. Leave port 4003 open between
       the OpenAVC server and the Base Unit.
    2. In the Base Unit's web Configurator (https://<base-unit>), open
       Security → Pin Code / API and confirm the API is enabled. Default
       credentials are integrator / integrator. Change them and supply
       the new ones below.
    3. (Recommended) Replace the self-signed HTTPS certificate with one
       trusted by the OpenAVC host, then flip "Verify SSL Certificate"
       on. The driver works either way; verifying is just defense in
       depth.
    4. Click Save. The driver polls every 30 seconds by default — drop
       to 10 s if you need faster sharing-state updates (the Base Unit
       can handle it; ClickShare's own integrations poll more frequently).

discovery:
  # ClickShare Base Units do not advertise a Barco-specific SSDP URN.
  # Barco KB7525 ("Order and precedence of ClickShare App discovery")
  # describes SSDP/mDNS as the transport but never quotes a
  # `urn:barco-...` device-type — every public deployment writeup and
  # third-party module addresses Base Units by IP/hostname, not by
  # URN match. The `_mirrorop2upc._tcp` mDNS string is documented in
  # Barco KB3896 but it's a wePresent/ClickShare family service and
  # too generic to claim as a positive signal alone.
  # Hint-only via OUI + factory hostname pattern (case-insensitive
  # to catch both `clickshare-…` and `ClickShare-…`).
  oui:
    - "00:04:a5"
  hostname:
    - "^[Cc]lick[Ss]hare-"
  manufacturer_alias:
    - "barco"
    - "clickshare"

default_config:
  host: ""
  port: 4003
  ssl: true
  verify_ssl: false
  auth_type: "basic"
  username: "integrator"
  password: "integrator"
  timeout: 5.0
  poll_interval: 30

config_schema:
  host:
    type: string
    required: true
    label: Base Unit IP Address
    description: "IP address (or hostname) of the ClickShare Base Unit."
  port:
    type: integer
    default: 4003
    label: HTTPS Port
    description: "REST API V2 port. Default 4003. The API is HTTPS only."
  username:
    type: string
    default: "integrator"
    required: true
    label: API Username
    description: "Default is 'integrator'. Change in the Base Unit's web Configurator under Security."
  password:
    type: string
    default: "integrator"
    required: true
    label: API Password
    description: "Default is 'integrator'. Change in the Base Unit's web Configurator."
    secret: true
  verify_ssl:
    type: boolean
    default: false
    label: Verify SSL Certificate
    description: >
      Off by default — the Base Unit ships with a self-signed certificate
      that won't verify. Replace the cert via Configurator → Security →
      HTTPS and turn this on for full TLS validation.
  poll_interval:
    type: integer
    default: 30
    min: 5
    label: Poll Interval (sec)
    description: "How often to refresh sharing / power / audio / video / wallpaper state."
  timeout:
    type: number
    default: 5.0
    label: Request Timeout (sec)

state_variables:

  # ── System status (configuration/system/status) ──
  in_use:
    type: boolean
    label: In Use
    help: "True when at least one source (Button or App) is connected to the Base Unit."
  sharing:
    type: boolean
    label: Sharing
    help: "True when at least one connected source is currently sharing content on the display."
  current_uptime:
    type: integer
    label: Current Uptime (sec)
    help: "Seconds since the Base Unit was last booted."
  total_uptime:
    type: integer
    label: Total Uptime (sec)
    help: "Total seconds the Base Unit has run across its lifetime."
  error_code:
    type: integer
    label: Error Code
    help: "Health code. 0 = OK; non-zero means errorMessage will explain."
  error_message:
    type: string
    label: Error Message
    help: "Health message. Empty when the Base Unit is healthy."

  # ── Power management (configuration/system/power-management) ──
  system_status:
    type: string
    label: System Status
    help: "Base Unit display-output power state — On or Standby."
  power_mode:
    type: string
    label: Power Mode
    help: "Selected standby mode: EcoStandby / NetworkedStandby / DeepStandby (set via set_power_mode)."
  standby_timeout:
    type: string
    label: Standby Timeout (min)
    help: "Inactivity timeout before entering standby — 'Infinite' or a numeric string of minutes."

  # ── Device identity (configuration/system/device-identity) ──
  product_name:
    type: string
    label: Product
    help: "User-facing model name, e.g. CX-30."
  model_name:
    type: string
    label: Platform
    help: "Internal platform name, e.g. C3010S."
  serial_number:
    type: string
    label: Serial Number
    help: "Base Unit serial number reported by configuration/system/device-identity."
  article_number:
    type: string
    label: Article Number
    help: "Barco SKU / article number, e.g. R9861511EU."

  # ── Audio (configuration/audio) ──
  audio_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: Audio Enabled
    help: "True when audio output is enabled on the Base Unit."
  audio_output:
    type: string
    label: Audio Output
    help: "Selected audio output: DisplayPort / Jack / HDMI / SPDIF (Base Unit-dependent)."

  # ── Video (configuration/video) ──
  video_mode:
    type: string
    label: Video Mode
    help: "Dual-output behavior — Extended or Clone (only meaningful on dual-output Base Units)."
  cec_enabled:
    type: boolean
    label: CEC Enabled
    help: "When true, the Base Unit reacts to CEC signals from connected displays."

  # ── Wallpaper (configuration/wallpapers/selected) ──
  selected_wallpaper_id:
    type: integer
    label: Wallpaper ID
    help: "ID of the wallpaper currently selected for display."
  selected_wallpaper_name:
    type: string
    label: Wallpaper Name
    help: "Display name of the currently-selected wallpaper."

commands:

  # ── Operations (operations/...) ──

  standby:
    label: Standby
    method: POST
    path: "/v2/operations/standby"
    help: "Put the Base Unit into standby. Display output disabled; behavior depends on power_mode."

  wakeup:
    label: Wake Up
    method: POST
    path: "/v2/operations/wakeup"
    help: "Wake the Base Unit from standby. Available since API 2.9."

  reboot:
    label: Reboot
    method: POST
    path: "/v2/operations/reboot"
    help: "Reboot the Base Unit. Briefly drops the API connection."

  # ── Status / identity queries ──

  query_status:
    label: Query System Status
    method: GET
    path: "/v2/configuration/system/status"
    help: "Refreshes in_use, sharing, uptime, error state."

  query_power:
    label: Query Power Management
    method: GET
    path: "/v2/configuration/system/power-management"
    help: "Refreshes system_status (On/Standby), power_mode, standby_timeout."

  query_identity:
    label: Query Device Identity
    method: GET
    path: "/v2/configuration/system/device-identity"
    help: "Refreshes product_name, model_name, serial_number, article_number. Static — runs once at connect."

  query_audio:
    label: Query Audio Settings
    method: GET
    path: "/v2/configuration/audio"
    help: "Refreshes audio_enabled, audio_output."

  query_video:
    label: Query Video Settings
    method: GET
    path: "/v2/configuration/video"
    help: "Refreshes video_mode, cec_enabled."

  query_wallpaper_selected:
    label: Query Selected Wallpaper
    method: GET
    path: "/v2/configuration/wallpapers/selected"
    help: "Refreshes selected_wallpaper_id, selected_wallpaper_name."

  query_wallpapers:
    label: List All Wallpapers
    method: GET
    path: "/v2/configuration/wallpapers"
    help: "Returns the wallpaper catalog as a JSON array — read the response to find IDs to use with select_wallpaper."

  query_buttons:
    label: List Paired Buttons
    method: GET
    path: "/v2/configuration/buttons"
    help: "Returns the array of paired ClickShare Buttons — connection state, IP, MAC, firmware, status."

  # ── Audio control (configuration/audio) ──

  audio_enable:
    label: Audio Enable
    method: PATCH
    path: "/v2/configuration/audio"
    body: '{"enabled": true}'
    help: "Enable the Base Unit's audio output. After flipping this, paired Buttons must be re-paired before the change takes effect."

  audio_disable:
    label: Audio Disable
    method: PATCH
    path: "/v2/configuration/audio"
    body: '{"enabled": false}'

  set_audio_output:
    label: Set Audio Output
    method: PATCH
    path: "/v2/configuration/audio"
    body: '{"output": "{output}"}'
    help: "Select the audio output. Only outputs in the Base Unit's supportedOutputs are valid; others return an error."
    params:
      output:
        type: enum
        values: ["DisplayPort", "Jack", "HDMI", "SPDIF"]
        default: "HDMI"
        required: true
        label: Output

  # ── Video control (configuration/video) ──

  set_video_mode:
    label: Set Video Mode
    method: PATCH
    path: "/v2/configuration/video"
    body: '{"mode": "{mode}"}'
    help: "Dual-output Base Units only. Extended = independent screens, Clone = mirrored."
    params:
      mode:
        type: enum
        values: ["Extended", "Clone"]
        default: "Extended"
        required: true
        label: Mode

  cec_enable:
    label: CEC Enable
    method: PATCH
    path: "/v2/configuration/video"
    body: '{"cecEnabled": true}'
    help: "Allow the Base Unit to react to CEC signals from the connected display. Requires cecConfigurable=true on the Base Unit (API 2.19+)."

  cec_disable:
    label: CEC Disable
    method: PATCH
    path: "/v2/configuration/video"
    body: '{"cecEnabled": false}'

  # ── Wallpaper control ──

  select_wallpaper:
    label: Select Wallpaper
    method: PATCH
    path: "/v2/configuration/wallpapers/selected"
    body: '{"id": {id}}'
    help: "Switch the active wallpaper. Run query_wallpapers first to get IDs."
    params:
      id:
        type: integer
        required: true
        default: 1
        min: 1
        label: Wallpaper ID

  # ── Power management ──

  set_power_mode:
    label: Set Power Mode
    method: PATCH
    path: "/v2/configuration/system/power-management"
    body: '{"powerMode": "{mode}"}'
    help: "EcoStandby = lowest power, no LAN wake. NetworkedStandby = LAN-wakeable. DeepStandby = deepest sleep."
    params:
      mode:
        type: enum
        values: ["EcoStandby", "NetworkedStandby", "DeepStandby"]
        default: "NetworkedStandby"
        required: true
        label: Power Mode

  set_standby_timeout:
    label: Set Standby Timeout
    method: PATCH
    path: "/v2/configuration/system/power-management"
    body: '{"standbyTimeout": "{timeout}"}'
    help: "Minutes of inactivity before standby, or 'Infinite' to disable auto-standby. Valid values are reported in supportedStandbyTimeouts."
    params:
      timeout:
        type: enum
        values: ["Infinite", "1", "5", "10", "15", "30", "45", "60"]
        default: "30"
        required: true
        label: Timeout (min)

# Response patterns. The V2 API returns JSON objects — match by field name.
# Field names are unique enough across the endpoints we poll that simple
# per-key regexes don't cross-fire. Notable choices:
#   - `"status":"(On|Standby)"` (anchored on the two valid values) only
#     matches the power-management response; per-button "status" values
#     are Ok / Error / Warning and don't alternate-match.
#   - `"output":"(DisplayPort|Jack|HDMI|SPDIF)"` is anchored on the audio
#     output enum so it doesn't capture stray "output" keys elsewhere.
#   - The wallpaper response is `{"id":N,"md5":"...","name":"..."}` — match
#     id and name in one regex with two captures so we set both atomically.
responses:

  # System status
  - match: '"currentUptime":\s*(\d+)'
    set: { current_uptime: "$1" }
  - match: '"totalUptime":\s*(\d+)'
    set: { total_uptime: "$1" }
  - match: '"errorCode":\s*(\d+)'
    set: { error_code: "$1" }
  - match: '"errorMessage":"([^"]*)"'
    set: { error_message: "$1" }
  - match: '"inUse":(true|false)'
    set: { in_use: "$1" }
  - match: '"sharing":(true|false)'
    set: { sharing: "$1" }

  # Power management
  - match: '"powerMode":"([^"]+)"'
    set: { power_mode: "$1" }
  - match: '"standbyTimeout":"([^"]+)"'
    set: { standby_timeout: "$1" }
  - match: '"status":"(On|Standby)"'
    set: { system_status: "$1" }

  # Device identity
  - match: '"articleNumber":"([^"]+)"'
    set: { article_number: "$1" }
  - match: '"modelName":"([^"]+)"'
    set: { model_name: "$1" }
  - match: '"productName":"([^"]+)"'
    set: { product_name: "$1" }
  - match: '"serialNumber":"([^"]+)"'
    set: { serial_number: "$1" }

  # Audio
  - match: '"enabled":(true|false),"output":"(DisplayPort|Jack|HDMI|SPDIF)"'
    set: { audio_enabled: "$1", audio_output: "$2" }
  - match: '"output":"(DisplayPort|Jack|HDMI|SPDIF)"'
    set: { audio_output: "$1" }

  # Video — `mode` is unique to the video endpoint among polled responses.
  # `cecEnabled` is anchored to its own field name.
  - match: '"cecEnabled":(true|false)'
    set: { cec_enabled: "$1" }
  - match: '"mode":"(Extended|Clone)"'
    set: { video_mode: "$1" }

  # Wallpaper selected — capture id + name in one shot.
  - match: '"id":\s*(\d+),"md5":"[^"]*","name":"([^"]+)"'
    set: { selected_wallpaper_id: "$1", selected_wallpaper_name: "$2" }

on_connect:
  - query_identity
  - query_status
  - query_power
  - query_audio
  - query_video
  - query_wallpaper_selected

polling:
  queries:
    - query_status
    - query_power
    - query_audio
    - query_video
    - query_wallpaper_selected

# ── SIMULATOR DEFINITION ──
simulator:
  initial_state:
    in_use: false
    sharing: false
    current_uptime: 12345
    total_uptime: 6543210
    error_code: 0
    error_message: ""
    system_status: "On"
    power_mode: "NetworkedStandby"
    standby_timeout: "30"
    product_name: "CX-30"
    model_name: "C3010S"
    serial_number: "1860000001"
    article_number: "R9861511EU"
    audio_enabled: true
    audio_output: "HDMI"
    video_mode: "Extended"
    cec_enabled: false
    selected_wallpaper_id: 1
    selected_wallpaper_name: "barco.jpg"

  delays:
    command_response: 0.02

  controls:
    - type: indicator
      key: product_name
      label: Product
    - type: indicator
      key: serial_number
      label: Serial Number
    - type: toggle
      key: in_use
      label: In Use
    - type: toggle
      key: sharing
      label: Sharing
    - type: indicator
      key: current_uptime
      label: Current Uptime (s)
    - type: indicator
      key: system_status
      label: System Status
    - type: indicator
      key: power_mode
      label: Power Mode
    - type: indicator
      key: standby_timeout
      label: Standby Timeout
    - type: toggle
      key: audio_enabled
      label: Audio Enabled
    - type: indicator
      key: audio_output
      label: Audio Output
    - type: indicator
      key: video_mode
      label: Video Mode
    - type: toggle
      key: cec_enabled
      label: CEC Enabled
    - type: indicator
      key: selected_wallpaper_id
      label: Wallpaper ID
    - type: indicator
      key: selected_wallpaper_name
      label: Wallpaper Name

  command_handlers:

    # GET /v2/configuration/system/status
    - match: '^GET /v2/configuration/system/status$'
      handler: |
        body = (
          '{'
          f'"currentUptime":{state["current_uptime"]},'
          f'"errorCode":{state["error_code"]},'
          f'"errorMessage":"{state["error_message"]}",'
          '"firstUsed":"2023-01-15 12:00:00",'
          f'"inUse":{"true" if state["in_use"] else "false"},'
          f'"sharing":{"true" if state["sharing"] else "false"},'
          f'"totalUptime":{state["total_uptime"]}'
          '}'
        )
        respond(body)

    # GET /v2/configuration/system/power-management
    - match: '^GET /v2/configuration/system/power-management$'
      handler: |
        body = (
          '{'
          f'"powerMode":"{state["power_mode"]}",'
          f'"standbyTimeout":"{state["standby_timeout"]}",'
          f'"status":"{state["system_status"]}",'
          '"supportedPowerModes":["EcoStandby","NetworkedStandby","DeepStandby"],'
          '"supportedStandbyTimeouts":["Infinite","1","5","10","15","30","45","60"],'
          '"supportedStatuses":["On","Standby"]'
          '}'
        )
        respond(body)

    # GET /v2/configuration/system/device-identity
    - match: '^GET /v2/configuration/system/device-identity$'
      handler: |
        body = (
          '{'
          f'"articleNumber":"{state["article_number"]}",'
          '"hardwareVersion":"2.0",'
          f'"modelName":"{state["model_name"]}",'
          f'"productName":"{state["product_name"]}",'
          f'"serialNumber":"{state["serial_number"]}"'
          '}'
        )
        respond(body)

    # GET /v2/configuration/audio
    - match: '^GET /v2/configuration/audio$'
      handler: |
        body = (
          '{'
          f'"enabled":{"true" if state["audio_enabled"] else "false"},'
          f'"output":"{state["audio_output"]}",'
          '"supportedOutputs":["DisplayPort","Jack","HDMI","SPDIF"]'
          '}'
        )
        respond(body)

    # PATCH /v2/configuration/audio  — body may be {"enabled":...} or {"output":...}
    - match: '^PATCH /v2/configuration/audio\|(.*)$'
      handler: |
        body = match.group(1)
        if '"enabled": true' in body or '"enabled":true' in body:
          state["audio_enabled"] = True
        elif '"enabled": false' in body or '"enabled":false' in body:
          state["audio_enabled"] = False
        m = re.search(r'"output":\s*"([^"]+)"', body)
        if m:
          state["audio_output"] = m.group(1)
        respond('{}')

    # GET /v2/configuration/video
    - match: '^GET /v2/configuration/video$'
      handler: |
        body = (
          '{'
          '"autoDetect":true,'
          '"cecConfigurable":true,'
          f'"cecEnabled":{"true" if state["cec_enabled"] else "false"},'
          f'"mode":"{state["video_mode"]}",'
          '"supportedModes":["Extended","Clone"]'
          '}'
        )
        respond(body)

    # PATCH /v2/configuration/video
    - match: '^PATCH /v2/configuration/video\|(.*)$'
      handler: |
        body = match.group(1)
        if '"cecEnabled": true' in body or '"cecEnabled":true' in body:
          state["cec_enabled"] = True
        elif '"cecEnabled": false' in body or '"cecEnabled":false' in body:
          state["cec_enabled"] = False
        m = re.search(r'"mode":\s*"([^"]+)"', body)
        if m:
          state["video_mode"] = m.group(1)
        respond('{}')

    # PATCH /v2/configuration/system/power-management
    - match: '^PATCH /v2/configuration/system/power-management\|(.*)$'
      handler: |
        body = match.group(1)
        m = re.search(r'"powerMode":\s*"([^"]+)"', body)
        if m:
          state["power_mode"] = m.group(1)
        m = re.search(r'"standbyTimeout":\s*"([^"]+)"', body)
        if m:
          state["standby_timeout"] = m.group(1)
        respond('{}')

    # GET /v2/configuration/wallpapers/selected
    - match: '^GET /v2/configuration/wallpapers/selected$'
      handler: |
        body = (
          '{'
          f'"id":{state["selected_wallpaper_id"]},'
          '"md5":"6f34fedd3c91a130fde57b7c76ab44f5",'
          f'"name":"{state["selected_wallpaper_name"]}"'
          '}'
        )
        respond(body)

    # PATCH /v2/configuration/wallpapers/selected
    - match: '^PATCH /v2/configuration/wallpapers/selected\|(.*)$'
      handler: |
        body = match.group(1)
        m = re.search(r'"id":\s*(\d+)', body)
        if m:
          new_id = int(m.group(1))
          state["selected_wallpaper_id"] = new_id
          state["selected_wallpaper_name"] = f"wallpaper_{new_id}.jpg"
        respond('{}')

    # GET /v2/configuration/wallpapers — return a small catalog.
    - match: '^GET /v2/configuration/wallpapers$'
      handler: |
        respond(
          '['
          '{"id":1,"md5":"6f34fedd3c91a130fde57b7c76ab44f5","name":"barco.jpg"},'
          '{"id":2,"md5":"3d8644944f358d3ef2d466c683255328","name":"meeting.jpg"}'
          ']'
        )

    # GET /v2/configuration/buttons — single fake paired Button.
    - match: '^GET /v2/configuration/buttons$'
      handler: |
        respond(
          '['
          '{"connected":false,"connectionCount":42,"firmwareVersion":"04.05.00",'
          '"id":1,"ipAddress":"192.168.2.10","lastConnected":"2024-01-10 10:00:00",'
          '"lastPaired":"2023-09-01 14:00:00","macAddress":"00:11:22:33:44:55",'
          '"modelInfo":"GEN4.0","productId":"0x0114","serialNumber":"1860000099",'
          '"status":"Ok","supportedUsbIdentifierModes":["Default","Room"],'
          '"usbIdentifierMode":"Default","vendorId":"0x2EBD"}'
          ']'
        )

    # POST /v2/operations/standby
    - match: '^POST /v2/operations/standby(\|.*)?$'
      handler: |
        state["system_status"] = "Standby"
        respond('')

    # POST /v2/operations/wakeup
    - match: '^POST /v2/operations/wakeup(\|.*)?$'
      handler: |
        state["system_status"] = "On"
        respond('')

    # POST /v2/operations/reboot
    - match: '^POST /v2/operations/reboot(\|.*)?$'
      handler: |
        state["current_uptime"] = 0
        respond('')
